Package: bayescompRLLVM
Type: Package
Title: LLVM Native Code Backend for 'bayescompR'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Adam R", "Sophie", email = "adamrsophie@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Compiles the typed intermediate representation of a 'bayescompR'
    model to machine code with the LLVM compiler infrastructure and
    evaluates the log density and its gradient natively. Registers the
    backend "llvm" with 'bayescompR'; the reference interpreter of the shared
    native runtime is available as an engine for comparison.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://github.com/adamrsophie/bayescomp-native-rs
BugReports: https://github.com/adamrsophie/bayescomp-native-rs/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports: bayescompR (>= 0.1.0)
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Remotes: adamrsophie/bayescompR
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.85, LLVM 18, 20, 21 or 22
    (development files, found through llvm-config or the LLVM_CONFIG variable); Linux or macOS
OS_type: unix
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
